keyswap (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recover per-device key state after evdev reports dropped events.
  * Prevent the virtual keyboard from creating a second repeat source.
  * Exclude ydotool's virtual device from automatic keyboard discovery.
  * Limit periodic discovery scans to systems without inotify support.

 -- Bene <bene@bjnobre.com>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400

keyswap (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the text-expansion config key from sequences to expansions.
  * Reject the removed sequences config key.
  * Use expansion terminology throughout the runtime and documentation.

 -- Bene <bene@bjnobre.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400

keyswap (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add commands to list, add, and delete substitutions and expansions.
  * Add configuration validation and atomic updates.
  * Add user-service controls and journal-backed history.
  * Install the keyswap command-line launcher.

 -- Bene <bene@bjnobre.com>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400

keyswap (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package.
  * Declare the adduser and libxkbcommon0 runtime dependencies.
  * Apply udev permission changes to existing devices on install and removal.
  * Refer users to README.Debian for post-installation setup.

